  "plot_summary": "[HANG0] * Paul Gambaccini's letter printed in [LINK:1963:ASM_7|ASM #7|2027-01-21] was perhaps the first case of calling the competition \"[SPAN: severity=error; fonttype=bold; text=echh].\"&nbsp; It's a small moment, but it hints at the playful rivalry tone Marvel is already cultivating.\n\n[HANG0] * The Announcements at the end of [LINK:1963:ASM_7|ASM #7|2027-01-21] actually asks permission to <i>discontinue the letters page</i> in ASM, indicating that it takes a good while to put together -- a surprising admission for a feature that's quickly becoming a hallmark of their books.\n[BR]\n[BR] It even suggests that comments about <i>all</i> magazines be instead directed to the FF mag, indicating:&nbsp; <i>We'll do nothing till we hear from you, so let us know.&nbsp; But, as a special favor, we hope you'll tell us you don't mind.</i>\n[BR]\n[BR] [SPAN: severity=warning; text=(Boy, I'll bet <i>that</i> went over like a lead balloon -- <i>wow</i>!)]\n\n[ASSET: right | AvengersNextIssue | width=22%] [HANG0] * In light of Iron Man's new armor introduced in this month's [LINK:1963:TOS_48_iron0|TOS #48|2027-02-02], the full-page ad in this month's [LINK:1963:AVEN_2|AVEN #2|2027-01-09] already looks stale.&nbsp; It's an accidental snapshot of how fast the line is evolving month to month.\n[BR]\n[BR] It correctly indicates that the Sub-Mariner will feature in the next issue, but still shows Iron Man wearing his older armor.&nbsp; You can clearly see which issue was published first, the ad presumably drawn before it was known that Iron Man would redesign his suit.&nbsp; (For the record, AVEN #3 does not get published until November, a full two months after this month's issue 2.)\n[BR]\n[BR] [SPAN: fontsize=small; text=(And since <i>Avengers</i> is a title, the word should be the singular \"<b>features</b>\" rather than \"feature,\" but let's not get nit-picky, because then I'd have to point out that the Hulk's head shouldn't be there... because he just <i>quit</i>!&nbsp; And I <i>really</i> don't want to have to do that, <i>wink...</i>)]",
